index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7488bf8b3f8d46fa77e5b8c18d2f52d719208ed8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/assets/generated/directions/D2.prompt.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Use case: ui-mockup
+Create one finished Crownforge BOOMTOOTH 2D slot game art-direction mockup. Exactly 1536 x 1024 pixels landscape, opaque full-bleed background.
+HOUSE STYLE: adult comic/cartoon 2D, thick slightly irregular black brush-ink contours (4–7 px at 1536 width), finer interior marks, simple immediately readable silhouettes. Strict two-tone cel shading, one crisp off-white highlight per volume, controlled saturated colors and warm neutrals. Draw materials with hatching and graphic spots, never photo textures. No photorealism, smooth/plastic 3D, generic neon, default gradients, airbrush, blur, bloom, bokeh, border effects, system fonts, emoji, or square dashboard panels. Original characters/composition, no other studio imitation.
+SCENE: vain daredevil beaver foreman Buck is blasting a granite mountain into a monument of his own beaver face above a log dam in a northern pine valley.
+LAYOUT: scenery behind; dominant FRONT-FACING SQUARE grid centered slightly left, entire grid fully visible, exactly FIVE columns and FIVE rows = 25 separate SQUARE cells. Reserve roughly x=220..945 y=175..900 for this square. Game logo above the grid toward its upper left, illustrated carved/plank lettering with fuse/spark: "BOOMTOOTH". Full-body Buck stands on the ground to the right, entirely visible with contact shadow. Compact HUD across bottom within frame: illustrated left button "BUY BONUS", exactly three empty value plaques (balance, bet, win) with no words/numerals; minus and plus icon controls flank middle plaque. Large round "SPIN" button at bottom right, a few small round icon-only buttons. Keep logo, Buck, HUD uncropped, readable, with breathing room.
+BUCK invariant: stocky muscular russet-brown beaver, big flat visibly scaly tail, exactly two upper front incisors, HIS LEFT FRONT INCISOR GOLD (viewer-right in frontal view), other ivory. Dented orange construction helmet with headlamp, red-and-black plaid shirt rolled sleeves, suspenders, tool belt, match at mouth corner. Proud mischievous raised eyebrows and wide grin showing gold tooth. One boot on a crate, one hand on wooden plunger detonator handle, other hand holding red dynamite stick with lit fuse. Keep both hands and props legible.
+GRID SYMBOLS: each cell darker than scenery; one large fully contained icon 85–95% cell size, thick black outlines, repeated families clearly consistent. Four low icons: yellow hardhat; blue-handled pickaxe; green lantern; purple metal canteen. Four high icons, expressive head-and-bust animal crew: raccoon explosives expert with natural black eye-mask and welding goggles, smirk; burly moose with large antlers; otter surveyor with rolled blueprint and pencil behind ear; woodpecker driller with helmet and drill bit. WILD is golden dynamite crate labeled exactly "WILD"; SCATTER is red dynamite bundle with detonator labeled exactly "SCATTER"; special dynamite is single red stick with short fuse and NO writing.
+Use this precise 5x5 arrangement, with no row labels:
+row 1: yellow hardhat | raccoon | blue-handled pickaxe | moose | green lantern
+row 2: otter | golden WILD crate | purple canteen | woodpecker | red SCATTER bundle
+row 3: green lantern | single dynamite | moose | yellow hardhat | raccoon
+row 4: blue-handled pickaxe | woodpecker | red SCATTER bundle | otter | purple canteen
+row 5: golden WILD crate | purple canteen | yellow hardhat | single dynamite | green lantern
+TEXT: Only "BOOMTOOTH", "BUY BONUS", "SPIN", "WILD", "SCATTER", verbatim and clearly legible, with plus/minus pictograms allowed. No other letters, numbers, captions, signature, watermark, or Crownforge wordmark. No written TNT, no direction label.
+DIRECTION D2 — Pop lumberjack screen-printed poster. Very flat, bold graphic cut-paper layers; halftone dots only within shadow areas. Reduced palette plaid red #C8312B, cream #F1E3C2, midnight blue #1F2B45, pine green #3C6E4F, gold #E9B03A. Sawtooth mountains, triangular pines, radiating sun behind the mountain carved as Buck's beaver head. Balanced symmetrical environmental composition, strong poster geometry. Grid frame is a giant pale wooden dynamite crate of nailed planks with reinforced metal corners. No outer poster border. Logo above grid on left. Crisp flat light and hard graphic silhouettes.
+CORRECTIONS FOR FINAL D2: Make the 25 cells truly SQUARE: grid inner area exactly 680 px wide and 680 px tall, five equal 136 px columns and rows. Enforce much flatter screen-print cut-paper geometry, large plain cream/red/navy shapes, stylized TRIANGULAR pine trees and SAWTOOTH mountain paper layers, not intricately rendered scenery. Halftone dots confined to shadow shapes. Simplify all drawn texture. The plunger detonator at Buck's foot must be a natural WOODEN box with wood grain, not red metal. Keep all five exact texts and all eleven symbol families, Buck's gold tooth and full silhouette.

